# Issue #239: primitive method return-type inference was DEAD, and had been since commit
# 7dc04567 removed the last semantics->backend import from the validation path. That import
# was also the accidental side effect that populated the builtin-method registry before
# Pass 2 ran, so check_primitive_methods has been reading an EMPTY registry ever since --
# it returned no inferrer, nothing typed the call, and the mismatch reached codegen:
# `CE0017: cannot convert value of type '{i8*, i32, i8}' to 'i32'`.
#
# No test caught it because tests/unit/test_primitive_methods.py imports the backend itself
# (warming the registry) and only asserts method NAMES, never return types. This test goes
# through the real compile path, where the registry is cold. `.to_str()` returns string.
# EXPECT_ERROR_CODE: CE2002

fn main() i32:
    let i32 n = 5
    let i32 bad = n.to_str()
    println(bad)
    return Result.Ok(0)
